# code/src/scripts/audits/docs-pairing.exempt — directories that need no CONTEXT.md + CLAUDE.md pair.
#
# Read by docs-pairing.sh. One bash `[[ == ]]` glob per line, matched against each
# directory's repo-relative path with no trailing slash; the repository root is ".".
# In these globs `*` also matches "/", so "learning/*" covers every level below learning/
# but not learning/ itself, which keeps its pair. Blank lines and lines starting with #
# are ignored.
#
# The exemption CLASSES, and the reason for each, are owned by
# code/docs/DOCUMENTATION-PAIRING.md; this file is only their machine-readable form.
# Add a line here only alongside a matching change there.

# The repository root: the manual is .claude/CLAUDE.md, so the root carries CONTEXT.md only.
.

# Git internals.
.git
.git/*

# GitHub configuration: issue and PR templates and CI workflows, read by GitHub.
.github
.github/*

# Skill folders: each SKILL.md is the folder's own orientation.
.claude/skills/*

# Build output: never committed, regenerated by every build (make's build/, Cargo's target/).
build
build/*
*/build
*/build/*
target
target/*
*/target
*/target/*

# Support folders covered by the pair in their parent directory.
code/src/c/mk
code/src/c/include
code/src/scripts/*
code/src/c/ms*/*
code/src/rust/crates
code/src/rust/crates/*/*

# Sandbox content below each session layer (the layer root itself keeps its pair).
learning/*
research/*
handoffs/*
